From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: The driver's allocations count once in the memory
 budget

The memory budget adds allocated_vram and allocated_vram_vis for an
APU's visible heap. The console's heap information set both to the
driver's allocations, so every allocation counted twice: a game with
5 GiB of video memory read 10, DXVK's report showed twice the memory in
use as reserved, and Unreal warned on screen that video memory was
exhausted. The driver's allocations are all in the visible heap, the
only one with device-local memory, so allocated_vram stays 0.
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
index e9fa953..f7658fc 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
@@ -3266,10 +3266,14 @@ radv_query_heap_info(struct radv_physical_device *pdev, struct radeon_winsys_hea
    memset(heap_info, 0, sizeof(*heap_info));
 #ifdef RADV_PS5
    /* One pool, which the CPU draws on too: the driver's own allocations and
-    * what the pool has handed out to anyone. */
+    * what the pool has handed out to anyone. The driver's are all in the
+    * visible heap, the only one with device-local memory: the budget adds
+    * allocated_vram and allocated_vram_vis for an APU, so the first stays 0,
+    * or every allocation counted twice (a game with 5 GiB of video memory
+    * read 10, and Unreal warned that video memory was exhausted). */
    uint64_t pool = 0, available = 0, driver = 0;
    radv_ps5_winsys_heap_usage(&pool, &available, &driver);
-   heap_info->allocated_vram = driver;
+   heap_info->allocated_vram = 0;
    heap_info->allocated_vram_vis = driver;
    heap_info->vram_usage = pool - MIN2(available, pool);
    heap_info->vram_vis_usage = heap_info->vram_usage;
